Alternative for CLI-01: do not parse -m in the option loop; only remember the
pointer, and after the exclusivity check do `if (straptr != NULL)
SCOTCH_stratDgraphMap(&stradat, straptr); else { Build... }' (the gmap.c
structure). Also removes the redundant Exit/Init pair. Slightly larger diff;
same user-visible behaviour as the recommended guard. Not chosen because the
minimal guard is a smaller, lower-risk change matching dgord.c.

--- a/src/scotch/dgmap.c (sketch)
+++ b/src/scotch/dgmap.c
@@ option 'm' @@
           straptr = &argv[i][2];
-          SCOTCH_stratExit (&stradat);
-          SCOTCH_stratInit (&stradat);
-          SCOTCH_stratDgraphMap (&stradat, straptr);
           break;
@@ before SCOTCH_contextBindDgraph @@
-  if ((flagval & C_FLAGCLUSTER) != 0)
-    SCOTCH_stratDgraphClusterBuild (...);
-  else
-    SCOTCH_stratDgraphMapBuild (...);
+  if (straptr != NULL)
+    SCOTCH_stratDgraphMap (&stradat, straptr);
+  else if ((flagval & C_FLAGCLUSTER) != 0)
+    SCOTCH_stratDgraphClusterBuild (...);
+  else
+    SCOTCH_stratDgraphMapBuild (...);
